  <main>
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="shell hero-grid">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow">AI Representation Infrastructure</div>
          <h1>Publish a source of truth—and keep it accurate.</h1>
          <p class="hero-copy">VizAI turns your business and product facts into clear, structured, machine-readable infrastructure, then monitors how selected AI systems represent those facts over time.</p>
          <div class="button-row">
            <a class="button" href="/scan">Run the free scan</a>
            <a class="button-secondary" href="#how-it-works">See how VizAI works</a>
          </div>
          <p class="hero-note">Improves the quality, consistency, and accessibility of business information. AI-system outcomes vary.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="truth-console" aria-label="Illustrative VizAI Truth Profile preview">
          <div class="console-bar">
            <span>VizAI Truth Profile · Illustrative record</span>
            <span class="console-status">Validated today</span>
          </div>
          <div class="console-grid">
            <section class="console-panel">
              <div class="panel-kicker">Canonical business record</div>
              <div class="record-head">
                <span class="record-mark">N</span>
                <div>
                  <strong>Northstar Logistics Inc.</strong>
                  <small>Record V1.4 · Toronto, Canada</small>
                </div>
                <span class="verified-badge">Domain verified</span>
              </div>
              <div class="fact-list">
                <div class="fact-row"><span>Legal name</span><strong>Northstar Logistics Inc.</strong></div>
                <div class="fact-row"><span>Primary offering</span><strong>Freight brokerage and warehousing</strong></div>
                <div class="fact-row"><span>Service market</span><strong>Canada and United States</strong></div>
                <div class="fact-row"><span>Canonical URL</span><strong>northstarlogistics.example</strong></div>
              </div>
              <div class="provenance">
                <span>Approved provenance</span>
                <strong>Corporate website · Product documentation · Domain-owner submission</strong>
              </div>
            </section>

            <aside class="console-panel monitoring">
              <div class="panel-kicker">Representation monitor</div>
              <div class="monitor-stack">
                <div class="monitor-card good"><strong>Identity aligned</strong><small>Selected systems match the canonical business name.</small></div>
                <div class="monitor-card warning"><strong>One location conflict</strong><small>An older directory still lists a former office.</small></div>
                <div class="monitor-card"><strong>Product scope partial</strong><small>Two newer services are not consistently represented.</small></div>
                <div class="monitor-card"><strong>Next action</strong><small>Correct the stale listing and strengthen approved service sources.</small></div>
              </div>
            </aside>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="shell">
      <div class="trust-boundary">
        <span class="trust-icon" aria-hidden="true">i</span>
        <span><strong>Clear boundary:</strong> VizAI improves the quality, consistency, and accessibility of business information. It does not guarantee crawling, indexing, citation, ranking, recommendation, or model-output changes.</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="section" id="problem">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="section-head">
          <div class="section-kicker">The representation problem</div>
          <h2 class="section-title">AI answers inherit the gaps in your public information.</h2>
          <p class="section-copy">Your website, listings, product pages, and third-party sources rarely describe the business in exactly the same way. VizAI makes the approved facts explicit and shows where representation begins to drift.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="three-grid">
          <article class="info-card"><span class="card-icon">01</span><h3>Facts are fragmented</h3><p>Core identity, product, location, and service facts sit across pages and systems with no maintained canonical record.</p></article>
          <article class="info-card"><span class="card-icon">02</span><h3>Old sources persist</h3><p>Stale listings and copied descriptions can compete with the information your team considers current and correct.</p></article>
          <article class="info-card"><span class="card-icon">03</span><h3>Answers are variable</h3><p>Different systems, prompts, and dates can produce different representations. A single visibility score cannot explain why.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section tint" id="how-it-works">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="section-head center">
          <div class="section-kicker">How VizAI works</div>
          <h2 class="section-title">From scattered facts to maintained infrastructure.</h2>
          <p class="section-copy">A structured, evidence-led process with a clear human review point.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="workflow-grid">
          <article class="step-card"><span class="step-number">1</span><h3>Observe</h3><p>VizAI maps the business, products, market, domain, and available public sources.</p><span class="gate-label">VizAI prepared</span></article>
          <article class="step-card"><span class="step-number">2</span><h3>Draft the Canon</h3><p>Observed and declared facts enter a private Draft Truth Canon. Nothing is public yet.</p><span class="gate-label">Private draft</span></article>
          <article class="step-card"><span class="step-number">3</span><h3>Customer confirms</h3><p>The customer confirms, edits, removes, or marks each material fact as unsure.</p><span class="gate-label customer">Customer gate</span></article>
          <article class="step-card"><span class="step-number">4</span><h3>Evidence is checked</h3><p>Credentials, awards, licences, and regulated claims require authority-grade evidence.</p><span class="gate-label">VizAI reviewed</span></article>
          <article class="step-card"><span class="step-number">5</span><h3>Canon v1.0</h3><p>A versioned, customer-approved Canon becomes the private source for every derived asset.</p><span class="gate-label owner">VizAI approval</span></article>
          <article class="step-card"><span class="step-number">6</span><h3>Prepare public assets</h3><p>VizAI prepares the Business Passport, Registry Profile, Evidence Ledger, Schema Package, and change log.</p><span class="gate-label">VizAI prepared</span></article>
          <article class="step-card"><span class="step-number">7</span><h3>Review and publish</h3><p>VizAI reviews the clean public artifact. External publication remains human-approved.</p><span class="gate-label owner">VizAI approval</span></article>
          <article class="step-card"><span class="step-number">8</span><h3>Monitor and maintain</h3><p>VizAI runs the defined checks, prepares updates, and escalates exceptions for review.</p><span class="gate-label">VizAI managed</span></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section compact">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="section-head"><div class="section-kicker">Managed delivery</div><h2 class="section-title">VizAI carries the workload. People retain the decisions.</h2><p class="section-copy">VizAI prepares and substantially executes paid reports and service tasks. Customers confirm their business facts; deliverables and external actions pass a defined review and approval gate.</p></div>
        <div class="role-flow">
          <article class="role-card"><span>01 · Customer</span><h3>Declares and confirms</h3><p>Provides authoritative facts, answers questions, and supplies evidence where required.</p></article>
          <article class="role-card vizai"><span>02 · VizAI delivery</span><h3>Researches and prepares</h3><p>Builds the draft, runs checks, assembles evidence, and produces the proposed deliverable.</p></article>
          <article class="role-card"><span>03 · VizAI owner</span><h3>Reviews and approves</h3><p>Checks exceptions, claims, evidence, and recommended actions without doing the underlying production work.</p></article>
          <article class="role-card"><span>04 · Governed system</span><h3>Publishes or records</h3><p>Only after the required approval, the system releases the report, applies the update, or prepares the public artifact.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section dark" id="free-scan">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="section-head">
          <div class="section-kicker">Start with evidence</div>
          <h2 class="section-title">See where the representation breaks first.</h2>
          <p class="section-copy">The free check is an automated, directional scan. It is designed to surface a useful starting point, not deliver a final diagnosis.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="scan-stage">
          <form class="form-card" action="#" onsubmit="return false;">
            <div class="panel-kicker">Free AI Representation Check</div>
            <div class="form-grid">
              <div class="form-row">
                <div class="field-group"><label for="home-business">Business name</label><input id="home-business" type="text" placeholder="Northstar Logistics"></div>
                <div class="field-group"><label for="home-site">Website</label><input id="home-site" type="url" placeholder="https://example.com"></div>
              </div>
              <div class="field-group"><label for="home-offering">Primary product or service</label><input id="home-offering" type="text" placeholder="Freight brokerage"></div>
              <div class="form-row">
                <div class="field-group"><label for="home-market">Market or location</label><input id="home-market" type="text" placeholder="Canada"></div>
                <div class="field-group"><label for="home-email">Business email</label><input id="home-email" type="email" placeholder="you@company.com"></div>
              </div>
              <button class="button" type="submit">Run my free scan</button>
              <p class="form-note">Automated and directional. Human validation is available through the $495 Snapshot.</p>
            </div>
          </form>
          <div class="score-preview">
            <div class="panel-kicker">Illustrative result preview</div>
            <h3>Representation baseline</h3>
            <p>Three indicators organize what was observed and point to the next useful review.</p>
            <div class="score-grid">
              <div class="score-card"><span class="score-value band">Developing</span><span class="score-label">Findability</span><small>Approved facts appear across accessible sources, but no canonical record is present.</small><span class="score-basis">Basis: 4 approved-source surfaces reviewed</span></div>
              <div class="score-card"><span class="score-value band">Mostly aligned</span><span class="score-label">Fidelity</span><small>Identity is consistent; location and service details vary in the selected set.</small><span class="score-basis">Basis: 8 fact comparisons, 2 material gaps</span></div>
              <div class="score-card"><span class="score-value band">Needs structure</span><span class="score-label">Source Readiness</span><small>Important facts are present but fragmented and inconsistently structured.</small><span class="score-basis">Basis: no maintained machine-readable record</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="sample-finding"><span>Sample finding</span><strong>One older location is still present in a third-party directory and appears in one selected AI response.</strong></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="sample-report">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="section-head">
          <div class="section-kicker">A report you can act on</div>
          <h2 class="section-title">Show the evidence behind the assessment.</h2>
          <p class="section-copy">Every human-reviewed Snapshot connects observations to sources, impact, and a prioritized next step.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="report-shell">
          <div class="report-topbar"><strong>AI Representation Snapshot · Northstar Logistics</strong><span class="sample-badge">Illustrative sample</span></div>
          <div class="report-layout">
            <div class="report-summary">
              <div class="panel-kicker">Executive summary</div>
              <h3>Identity is clear. Location and service scope need attention.</h3>
              <p class="section-copy">Core business identity is supported, but one outdated location and two inconsistently described services create avoidable ambiguity.</p>
              <div class="report-score-row">
                <div class="mini-score"><strong>Moderate</strong><span>Data quality confidence</span></div>
                <div class="mini-score"><strong>Elevated</strong><span>Representation risk</span></div>
                <div class="mini-score"><strong>3</strong><span>Priority findings</span></div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="report-detail">
              <div class="panel-kicker">Priority findings</div>
              <div class="finding-line"><i>1</i><div><strong>Former office remains discoverable</strong><small>Update the directory record and make the current service area explicit in the canonical profile.</small></div></div>
              <div class="finding-line"><i>2</i><div><strong>Newer services lack supporting detail</strong><small>Publish concise service definitions with clear entity and market relationships.</small></div></div>
              <div class="finding-line"><i>3</i><div><strong>No maintained machine-readable record</strong><small>Create a versioned business and product data model with approved provenance.</small></div></div>
              <a class="button-quiet" href="/sample-report">Explore the sample report</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section tint" id="deliverables">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="section-head">
          <div class="section-kicker">What customers receive</div>
          <h2 class="section-title">A maintained information asset, not another abstract score.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="deliverable-grid">
          <article class="deliverable-card"><span class="deliverable-icon">01</span><h3>Private Truth Canon</h3><p>The versioned, customer-approved source that governs every other deliverable.</p></article>
          <article class="deliverable-card"><span class="deliverable-icon">02</span><h3>Business Passport</h3><p>A customer-facing view of approved identity, offers, locations, and operating facts.</p></article>
          <article class="deliverable-card"><span class="deliverable-icon">03</span><h3>Public Registry Profile</h3><p>A clean, public-safe, machine-readable subset with provenance and verification status.</p></article>
          <article class="deliverable-card"><span class="deliverable-icon">04</span><h3>Evidence and Schema Package</h3><p>The Evidence Ledger, relevant website structured data, and canonical change history.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="services">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="section-head">
          <div class="section-kicker">Service ladder</div>
          <h2 class="section-title">Start with the smallest useful commitment.</h2>
          <p class="section-copy">Validate the problem first. Build only when the evidence supports it. Maintain the infrastructure when the facts matter enough to keep current.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="service-grid" data-service-grid="check,snapshot,build,maintenance,managed,custom"></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section tint" id="ideal-customer">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="section-head">
          <div class="section-kicker">Best-fit organizations</div>
          <h2 class="section-title">Most useful when factual confusion has a real cost.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="audience-grid">
          <article class="audience-card"><span class="tag">Complex offers</span><h3>Multiple products or services</h3><p>Where categories, capabilities, and customer fit are often compressed or misunderstood.</p></article>
          <article class="audience-card"><span class="tag">Frequent change</span><h3>Evolving facts</h3><p>Where locations, teams, specifications, or availability change often enough to require maintenance.</p></article>
          <article class="audience-card"><span class="tag">Fragmented sources</span><h3>Conflicting public records</h3><p>Where directories, legacy pages, and third-party summaries compete with current information.</p></article>
          <article class="audience-card"><span class="tag">High consideration</span><h3>Trust-sensitive buying</h3><p>Where an inaccurate description can remove a business from consideration before direct contact.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section dark" id="maintenance">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="section-head">
          <div class="section-kicker">Recurring maintenance</div>
          <h2 class="section-title">Business facts change. The infrastructure should change with them.</h2>
          <p class="section-copy">VizAI provides a managed loop for keeping the record current and documenting what happens next.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="maintenance-loop">
          <div class="loop-step"><span>01 · Validate</span><strong>Check the infrastructure</strong><p>Confirm technical accessibility, record integrity, and approved source availability.</p></div>
          <div class="loop-step"><span>02 · Monitor</span><strong>Observe representation</strong><p>Run the defined query set across selected AI systems and record material changes.</p></div>
          <div class="loop-step"><span>03 · Maintain</span><strong>Process fact changes</strong><p>Update approved fields, relevant structured data, and the versioned Truth Profile.</p></div>
          <div class="loop-step"><span>04 · Report</span><strong>Document the work</strong><p>Summarize findings, alerts, corrections, open issues, and recommended next actions.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="registry">
      <div class="shell registry-preview">
        <div class="registry-copy">
          <div class="section-kicker">VizAI Business Registry</div>
          <h2 class="section-title">A public discovery layer for verified business facts.</h2>
          <p class="section-copy">The Registry publishes lightweight, structured records that link to richer business profiles and approved sources.</p>
          <div class="button-row"><a class="button-secondary" href="/registry">Preview the Registry</a></div>
        </div>
        <article class="registry-card">
          <div class="registry-card-head">
            <div class="registry-title"><span class="record-mark">N</span><div><strong>Northstar Logistics Inc.</strong><small>Transportation and logistics · Canada</small></div></div>
            <span class="status-badge">Verified record</span>
          </div>
          <div class="registry-facts">
            <div class="registry-fact"><span>Primary domain</span><strong>Verified</strong></div>
            <div class="registry-fact"><span>Record version</span><strong>V1.4</strong></div>
            <div class="registry-fact"><span>Last reviewed</span><strong>18 Jul 2026</strong></div>
          </div>
          <p class="registry-source"><strong>What verified means:</strong> Domain control was confirmed, public facts derive from the customer-confirmed Canon, and evidence-required claims passed authority-grade review. VizAI prepared and approved the record for publication. It is not an endorsement, ranking advantage, or guarantee of inclusion in an AI answer.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section tint" id="faq">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="section-head center"><div class="section-kicker">Common questions</div><h2 class="section-title">Clear scope. No outcome theatre.</h2></div>
        <div class="faq-list">
          <details><summary>Does VizAI guarantee citations or better AI answers?</summary><p>No. VizAI improves the quality, consistency, structure, and accessibility of approved business information. Crawling, indexing, retrieval, citation, ranking, and model output remain controlled by external systems.</p></details>
          <details><summary>What does VizAI verify?</summary><p>VizAI confirms control of the primary domain, derives public facts from the customer-confirmed Canon, and reviews evidence-required claims against authority-grade sources. Verification describes that governed process; it is not a general endorsement.</p></details>
          <details><summary>Is the platform self-serve software?</summary><p>No. VizAI performs the majority of defined service work. Customers confirm facts or supply required evidence, while paid deliverables and public actions move through defined review and approval gates in the portal.</p></details>
          <details><summary>Why start with a human-reviewed Snapshot?</summary><p>It establishes whether a meaningful problem exists, identifies the highest-priority gaps, and reduces the risk of investing in infrastructure without evidence. The fee can be credited toward a qualifying build within 30 days.</p></details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="shell final-cta">
      <div><h2>Start with a clear view of the facts.</h2><p>Run the automated check, then add human validation only if the result shows a meaningful representation gap.</p></div>
      <div class="button-row"><a class="button" href="/scan">Run the free scan</a><a class="button-secondary" href="/contact">Talk to VizAI</a></div>
    </section>
